# -*- coding: utf-8 -*-
C('uitje', "two adults seen whole-figure, front view, at one plain open doorway with a plain hall behind, a friend in a jacket stepping out over the threshold, same distance from the viewer, a flat floor line. Only the second adult changes: in a jacket stepping out beside the friend, or in slippers staying in the hall.",
  "Mijn vriend gaat mee naar het strand, maar ik blijf thuis.", "My friend goes along to the beach, but I stay at home.")
K('meegaan', "One drawing, one panel. Two adults in jackets step side by side out through the open doorway towards the viewer, both over the threshold, small arrows pointing forward. The hall behind them is bare and the door stands open.",
  "two walkers going out through the doorway side by side.",
  "one adult staying in the hall and waving at the doorway (thuisblijven); an adult carrying an umbrella through the door (meenemen); an adult walking alone away from a door (weggaan); a child pulling an adult by the hand (not the card).",
  "Pair with thuisblijven. The only difference is the second person: stepping out in a jacket beside the friend here, staying in the hall in slippers there.",
  "ga ... mee", "Ik ga met mijn vriend mee.", "I go along with my friend.", "is meegegaan",
  "Twee volwassenen met jassen lopen naast elkaar door een open deur naar buiten.")
K('thuisblijven', "One drawing, one panel. At the same open doorway the friend in a jacket steps out over the threshold towards the viewer, a small arrow pointing forward, while the second adult stays back in the hall in slippers and house clothes, no jacket, holding a mug.",
  "an adult in slippers with a mug staying in the hall as the friend steps out.",
  "both adults in jackets stepping out together (meegaan); an adult coming home through the door (thuiskomen); an adult lying asleep in bed (uitslapen); an adult relaxing on a sofa with no doorway (not the card).",
  "Pair with meegaan. The only difference is the second person: staying in the hall in slippers here, stepping out in a jacket beside the friend there.",
  "blijf ... thuis", "Ik blijf vandaag thuis.", "I am staying at home today.", "is thuisgebleven",
  "Een vriend met een jas stapt over de drempel naar buiten en een volwassene op sloffen staat met een mok in de gang.")

C('voordeur', "one plain house front door seen from the front with a doormat, a flat step and a plain wall, one adult in plain clothes, a bag in one hand, same distance from the viewer. Only whether the adult faces into the open door stepping in or faces out stepping away changes.",
  "Ik kom om zes uur thuis en mijn zus gaat om zeven uur weg.", "I come home at six o'clock and my sister goes away at seven o'clock.")
K('thuiskomen', "One drawing, one panel. An adult with a shopping bag stands on the doormat at the open front door, back to the viewer, one foot across the threshold into the house, small arrows pointing into the house. The hall inside is plain.",
  "one foot over the threshold, back to the viewer, arrows into the house.",
  "an adult stepping off the doorstep towards the viewer (weggaan); an adult ringing the doorbell outside (not the card); an adult stepping off a bus (uitstappen); an adult lying in bed at home (uitslapen).",
  "Pair with weggaan. The only difference is the direction: back turned and stepping in over the threshold here, facing out and stepping off the doorstep there.",
  "kom ... thuis", "Ik kom om zes uur thuis.", "I come home at six o'clock.", "is thuisgekomen",
  "Een volwassene met een boodschappentas staat met één voet over de drempel van een open voordeur.")
K('weggaan', "One drawing, one panel. An adult with a bag steps off the doorstep away from the open front door, face to the viewer, one foot already on the pavement, small arrows pointing away from the house towards the viewer. The doormat lies bare.",
  "face to the viewer, stepping off the doorstep, arrows away from the house.",
  "an adult stepping in over the threshold (thuiskomen); an adult staying on the sofa while a friend leaves (thuisblijven); a train leaving the platform (wegrijden); an adult running towards the door (not the card).",
  "Pair with thuiskomen. The only difference is the direction: facing out and stepping off the doorstep here, back turned and stepping in over the threshold there.",
  "ga ... weg", "Ik ga om zeven uur weg.", "I leave at seven o'clock.", "is weggegaan",
  "Een volwassene met een tas loopt bij een open voordeur vandaan, met het gezicht naar de straat.")

C('kaars', "one plain candle in a plain holder on a plain table, front view, whole object, same size on the page, one adult's hand, or for blowing the adult's face in profile, entering from the side, a plain wall behind. Only whether a small flame sits on the wick or thin smoke rises from the wick changes.",
  "Ik steek de kaars aan en later blaas ik hem weer uit.", "I light the candle and later I blow it out again.")
K('aansteken', "One drawing, one panel. A hand holds a lit match to the wick of a plain candle in a holder, and a small teardrop flame with three short glow lines stands on the wick. The match is tilted towards the wick and the wax below is smooth.",
  "a small flame on the wick and a match tipped towards it.",
  "the flame being blown out with smoke rising (uitblazen); a candle already burning with nobody near it (not the card); an adult switching on a lamp (aandoen); a match burning alone in a hand (not the card).",
  "Pair with uitblazen. The only difference is the wick: a flame on it with a match here, a thin curl of smoke and no flame there.",
  "steek ... aan", "Ik steek de kaars aan.", "I light the candle.", "heeft aangestoken",
  "Een hand houdt een lucifer bij het kaarsje en er brandt een klein vlammetje.")
K('uitblazen', "One drawing, one panel. An adult's face in profile on the left blows towards a plain candle in a holder with puffed cheeks and three short air lines. There is no flame: one thin wavy curl of smoke rises from the wick.",
  "puffed cheeks, air lines and a thin smoke curl from the wick.",
  "a match being held to the wick with a flame (aansteken); a candle snuffed with a cap and no breath (not the card); an adult blowing up a balloon (not the card); an adult switching off a lamp (uitdoen).",
  "Pair with aansteken. The only difference is the wick: a thin curl of smoke after a breath here, a flame and a match there.",
  "blaas ... uit", "Ik blaas de kaars uit.", "I blow out the candle.", "heeft uitgeblazen",
  "Een gezicht in profiel heeft bolle wangen bij een kaarsje en er kringelt een dun draadje rook omhoog.")

C('kraan', "one plain wall tap over a plain basin seen from the front, one adult's hand on the tap handle entering from the side, same size on the page, a plain wall behind. Only whether a column of water runs from the spout into the basin or not changes.",
  "Ik draai de kraan open en daarna draai ik hem dicht.", "I turn on the tap and then I turn it off.")
K('opendraaien', "One drawing, one panel. A hand turns the tap handle with a small curved arrow, and a straight column of water with three splash dots runs from the spout into the basin, a ripple ring where it lands.",
  "a straight water column from the spout with a ripple in the basin.",
  "the tap with no water and a hand on the handle (dichtdraaien); a rain cloud over the basin (not the card); a bucket being poured out (not the card); a hand holding a plug over the basin (not the card).",
  "Pair with dichtdraaien. The only difference is the spout: a water column with ripples here, a dry spout and a plain basin there.",
  "draai ... open", "Ik draai de kraan open.", "I turn on the tap.", "heeft opengedraaid",
  "Een hand pakt het handvat van een kraan en er stroomt een rechte straal water in de wasbak.")
K('dichtdraaien', "One drawing, one panel. A hand turns the same tap handle with a small curved arrow, a single drop hangs at the end of the spout and the basin below is plain with a few leftover droplets at the bottom. No water column.",
  "a dry spout with one hanging drop and a hand on the handle.",
  "a straight water column running from the tap (opendraaien); a hand plugging the basin drain (not the card); a hand wiping a sink with a cloth (schoonmaken); a leaking tap with a drip stream (not the card).",
  "Pair with opendraaien. The only difference is the spout: dry with one drop here, a full water column there.",
  "draai ... dicht", "Ik draai de kraan dicht.", "I turn off the tap.", "heeft dichtgedraaid",
  "Een hand zit op het handvat van een kraan en er glinstert nog één druppel aan de tuit.")

C('kaart', "one plain paper map with a few plain lines and one plain road, two hands holding it at the edges, front view, same distance from the viewer, a plain table behind. Only whether the sheet is a small folded block or opened flat changes.",
  "Ik vouw de kaart op en later vouw ik hem weer uit.", "I fold up the map and later I unfold it again.")
K('opvouwen', "One drawing, one panel. Two hands hold a map that is folded into a small thick stack of three flat layers, the fold edges visible on both sides, a small arrow showing the sheet's sides going inward. The folded map is about the size of one hand.",
  "a small thick stack of three flat layers held in two hands.",
  "the same map spread flat and wide (uitvouwen); a map rolled into a tube (not the card); a map crumpled in a ball (weggooien); a folded shirt in a case (inpakken).",
  "Pair with uitvouwen. The only difference is the sheet: folded into a small stack here, spread wide and flat there.",
  "vouw ... op", "Ik vouw de kaart op.", "I fold up the map.", "heeft opgevouwen",
  "Twee handen houden een papieren kaart vast die tot een klein dik pakketje van drie lagen is samengedrukt.")
K('uitvouwen', "One drawing, one panel. Two hands hold the same map spread wide and flat, a plain road line running across it and the fold creases forming a grid of small rectangles, arms stretched and a small arrow pointing outward on each side.",
  "a wide flat sheet with grid creases and outward arrows.",
  "the same map folded into a small stack (opvouwen); a map held crumpled in a fist (not the card); a newspaper being read (not the card); a tablecloth being laid on a table (not the card).",
  "Pair with opvouwen. The only difference is the sheet: spread wide and flat with creases here, folded into a small stack there.",
  "vouw ... uit", "Ik vouw de kaart uit.", "I unfold the map.", "heeft uitgevouwen",
  "Twee handen houden een papieren kaart wijd en vlak open en er lopen rechte kreuken in rechthoeken overheen.")
